        ("What is MVCC?", "Multi-Version Concurrency Control keeps row versions so readers and writers do not block each other."),
        ("PostgreSQL vs MySQL?", "PostgreSQL has richer SQL features, extensions and types (jsonb, arrays); MySQL is simpler and widely used."),
        ("What is VACUUM?", "Removes dead row versions and updates statistics to reclaim space."),
        ("What index types exist?", "B-tree, Hash, GIN, GiST, SP-GiST, BRIN."),
        ("`json` vs `jsonb`?", "`jsonb` is binary, indexable and faster to query; `json` stores exact text."),
